 goodbye to their childhoods like  it kind of reminds me of that famous  shot from one of the final episodes of  Mad Men with Peggy Olson dreamily  rollerskating around the office as they  pack things up and leave like this all  felt so sweet there should have been  some kind of music to celebrate this no  no not that not that music anyway this  adorable rollerskating leads to them  holding hands and then kissing whoa they  are way too young for that I'm saving my  first kiss for marriage it's gonna be so  hot now anyway this is all meant to show  they're coming of age their childhood is  officially ending and now with these  hormonal romantic sparks they're  becoming official adults and now they  feel the same grief and do the same  blindly reckless boasts that adults  sometimes do now moving on when Maggie  finds Enid at Glen's grave and she sees  in its green balloons that gives Maggie  the sense of relief that Jesus said the  color green would earlier now she's  actually come to return Herschel's watch  to Glenn's grave but now she realized  that she doesn't need these physical  tokens to remember him by because she  shares Glen's memory with Enid now I  love how the next scene reveals that  Enid tie those balloons to the wrong  grave which is hilarious because I was  imagining Sasha just like charging up  the Gregory like burst you steal the  watch from Glenn's grave then you throw  a party on Abraham's plate you son of a  [ __ ] now Maggie proves that she  understands what Jesus said about  keeping the memory of our dead loved  ones and ourselves not in physical  objects echoing what he said earlier we  don't need anything  we have us but this scene ending with  these three women praying again reminds  me of that biblical reference I  discussed earlier but from a purely  historical perspective Jesus Christ was  a martyr who was crucified whose message  of love and community inspired a  movement starting with the mourners who  first preached that narrative  similarly Glenn I think will live on in  the walking dead as a martyr with Maggie  and the others doing acts in his name  but Wow Maggie  Enid may have found this place of  acceptance sasha hasn't we've seen how  colors are important this episode with  blue inspiring strength and green  inspiring release and now check out the  colors that are behind Sasha bright red  red is the color of passion sasha sent  Jesus to go find the Savior's compound  and she doesn't want Maggie to know so  my guess is she plans to be a go-getter  to attack them and she doesn't want  Maggie to join her or to try to stop her  sasha is still very much driven by  revenge and anger let's talk about these  closing images so as Maggie's prayer end  and we see the Savior's leave we hear  this foreboding sound of Sasha  sharpening her knife this is her version  of letting go of Abraham she's letting  the cigar burn just like the hilltoppers  burn their bodies and letting go of this  physical token but in doing so she's  embracing the devilish go-getter spirit  that Abraham championed  she's preparing to go to an extreme  Jesus and Karl proved to be the same  kind of reckless go-getters  so Jesus not only hops in the back of  the Savior's truck He pours out a bottle  of scotch that Simon lifted off Gregory  so why does he do this my guess is he's  hoping it will cause an argument between  the Savior's over who will drink it and  then he could use that distraction to  attack or maybe escape but we also get  this reveal of Karl in the truck - and  that sets up a storyline that is taken  directly from the comics  with Karl hiding in the back of the  truck on the way to the sanctuary and  the title of episode 7 which is two  episodes from now has been revealed as  sing me a song  now those of you who read the comics  might remember what this is a reference  to and it's looking like Carl's Ark the  season is about to get a lot more  interesting because Karl just like  Maggie Sasha  Enid Jesus and others they don't want to  be obedient weaklings who cower before  the saviors they want to go on the  offensive take initiative and be true  go-getters ok a few lingering questions  one do you think Simon actually knew  about the hilltops deal with Rick  so Gregory was working really hard to  play dumb without the satellite outposts  everyone died in there  Simon seemed to buy  then again if not Gregory how else would  Rick's people have known where the  satellite post was but now they figure  that Rick is under their control anyway  so they'll need to rock the boat and  replace Gregory who's still cowardly and  loyal to them and to where do you think  Rick and Michonne are going so Rick said  that he and Aaron were headed north to  scavenge for more stuff for negan but  Michonne was less clear  so my blind guess is that Rick and Aaron  could be on a collision course for the  kingdom while Michonne might be headed  towards the sanctuary or maybe she'll  run into Heath and Tara who are  obviously my favorite characters and I  cannot wait to catch up with them next  episode then again to be honest  based on these shots of Walker's covered  in sand plus the boat and a lot of  Masterson's new title slide Plus this  footage of next week's episode which I  don't want to show too much up because  it could be a spoiler this show might be  bringing in a whole new community that's  really only been mentioned briefly in  the comics so stay tuned next week's  episode could be very interesting okay  thanks for watching and let me know what  you think in the comments and check out  our breakdowns of the past Walking Dead  episodes including episodes one through  four of this season and please hit like  and subscribe to new rockstars and share  this video with all your friends you can  also contribute to us on patreon and  thanks so much to all of our current  donors you guys are the best for the  rest of you if you aren't currently a  patron we'd love your support you can  hit me up on 